WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.917
It's much easier now to gain fame.

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:05.833
But it's harder to last.

00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:08.792
You know, I want to be famous
like the Kardashians

00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:12.958
who are famous for just being famous.

00:00:16.708 --> 00:00:21.750
Fame, in its earliest forms,
is some sense that

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:24.167
human beings need
something beyond themselves.

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:30.500
So they almost invented gods as a way
of explaining what happened next.

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:33.500
And, if there are gods, there's going
to be contact with gods.

00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:35.583
Some people are going to be
closer to them than others.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:40.375
The word celebrity itself
in the 1400s

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.167
still meant the celebration
of the sacred.

00:00:51.042 --> 00:00:54.667
The period where
the nature of fame changed

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.083
from people attributing
god-like qualities to it

00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:00.083
was when Charles I was executed.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.583
Something big had changed.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.875
And part of that is
the sense of self-making

00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:07.125
that becomes prominent
at this period.

00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:09.417
The idea that you
don't have to be rich,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.792
you do not have to be an
aristocrat to be a person of fame.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:18.417
We begin to enter into a situation
where the people become celebrities.

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:28.333
He represents the cult of
personality that we now know today.

00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.750
Oscar really was a nascent celebrity.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:46.042
His philosophy of life was that the
point of life is self-realisation,

00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:48.083
just as the point of art
is self-expression.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.458
You have to bring
out what it is inside you.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:53.458
The famous people in the 1880s

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:57.542
were politicians, scientists,
doctors, writers.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.000
By 1920, it was
singers, sportsmen, actors.

00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:03.917
And the reason for that
is the invention of film,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.542
which gives you the illusion of being
in touch with somebody

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:11.875
and close to them and forming bonds
with them, without ever meeting them.

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:22.792
Warhol was at the time, in the 60s,
creating this real buzz around him,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.167
and creating this iconic figure
that people flocked to.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.417
And he certainly influenced the people
and the scene around New York City. 

00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:36.667
And you could think about that today

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.458
with people who really
influence the social scene today -

00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:43.583
whether it might be somebody
like Kim Kardashian,

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:47.792
and the followers that she has, who
want to look like her physically.

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:53.167
There's a draw to
wanting to be that figure,

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.333
wanting to be that famous. 

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.917
Think about Warhol right now in this
era that we live in

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.250
with everybody taking selfies and
these images of themselves,

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:11.667
and thinking back to Warhol when he
filmed himself eating a hamburger.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:19.000
I mean, he was one of the pioneers
of turning the camera on oneself.

00:03:19.208 --> 00:03:21.542
Think about Andy Warhol now
with an iPhone.

00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:24.458
That would be the best
Instagram account to follow, right?

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.542
Why so many people
are attracted to celebrities

00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:30.292
is that we live in an age
of profound anxiety.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.375
Part of that is wanting
acceptance and approval in life.

00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:37.333
You want to be accepted by people,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.000
and you want to be
approved by people.

00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:43.542
Who are the people that have paid most
to be accepted and approved?

00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:44.792
Celebrities.

00:03:52.958 --> 00:03:55.708
Some people document their life,
which means that they don't lie -

00:03:55.792 --> 00:03:57.542
they just have a camera rolling. 

00:03:57.625 --> 00:04:02.708
And some people create their life,
so they actually stage a picture.

00:04:02.792 --> 00:04:04.542
They actually stage an outfit. 

00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:07.042
I think that this will be
the difference between

00:04:07.125 --> 00:04:09.500
a good influencer
and a bad influencer.

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:12.500
You have to be real,
because people will feel that

00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.125
whatever you're telling them to do,

00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:17.000
if it's not real and if it doesn't
come from your heart

00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:20.208
and whatever you believe in,
they know.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:26.333
I strongly believe that
the more you go into

00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:29.708
the pieces of you that
most people would hide,

00:04:30.042 --> 00:04:32.500
the better of an influencer
you are going to be.

00:04:33.542 --> 00:04:36.208
The more you're sharing things
that people are like,

00:04:36.292 --> 00:04:39.083
"What? I'm that way too."

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.917
That's when people get excited.
That's when they want to follow you.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.583
And it could just be that this
smaller kind of fame -

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.042
this idea of finding
your niche or your tribe -

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:52.917
people may come
more and more to value

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.500
smaller, individual acts of kindness
and of love,

00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.792
and become celebrated for them.

